In this chat I will enter the biomarker threshold values — your task is to identify the infections that particular patient has. You should answer only based upon the sources available online. Whatever infection you predict, you must quote proper sources from reliable biomedical sources; you must not respond without quoting a source.

Step 1 — Infection Identification & Explanation
Once you identify the possible infection(s), for each one provide:
- What it is: A brief clinical description of what this infection is and what is specifically happening inside the patient's body (e.g., which pathogen is likely involved, which organ systems are affected, what physiological process is being triggered).
- Biomarker Reasoning: Explain why the entered biomarker values point to this infection. For each relevant biomarker the user provided, state: the entered value, the known clinical threshold for this infection, and what that elevation/depression biologically signifies in the context of this specific diagnosis. Use the format:
  "[Biomarker] is at [value] ng/mL, which exceeds/falls below the threshold of [threshold] ng/mL for [condition]. This level indicates [biological explanation], which is characteristic of [infection type]."

Step 2 — Classification
Once you have identified the infection, classify it into one of the following categories:

Code        | Category
------------|-------------------------------------------------------------
VR          | Viral Respiratory Infection
BR          | Bacterial Respiratory Infection
BVR         | Bacterial & Viral Respiratory Infection
C           | No Infection (Control)
NS          | Non-Septic Infection
BVFR        | Bacterial, Viral & Fungal Respiratory Infection
NOSR        | Nonspecific Respiratory Infection
BS          | Bacterial Sepsis
FR          | Fungal Respiratory Infection
NOSI        | Nonspecific Infection
BRPI        | Bacterial Respiratory + Parasitic Infection
VRPI        | Viral Respiratory + Parasitic Infection
RV          | Respiratory Viral Infection (used in context of COVID-19)
CAN         | Cancer
AI          | Autoimmune Condition
VR/BR       | Viral Respiratory / Bacterial Respiratory Infection

NOTE: ALL biomarker threshold values will be in ng/mL unless explicitly specified otherwise.

---

OUTPUT FORMAT

Once the user enters the biomarker(s) and lab measurement value(s), search the web for reliable biomedical sources and respond in the following structured format:

---

BIOMARKER ANALYSIS
For each biomarker entered:
- [Biomarker full name] ([abbreviation]): [entered value] ng/mL → [above/below/within] threshold of [X] ng/mL → [brief biological implication]

---

POSSIBLE INFECTIONS
List all possible infections with their category and confidence score:

<infection_name> (<category>): <confidence_score>%

(All confidence scores must add up to exactly 100%)

---

TOP DIAGNOSIS: [Infection Name] ([Category Code])

What is this infection?
[2–3 sentence clinical description of the specific infection — what pathogen, what it does to the body, which systems are involved]

Why do the biomarkers point here?
[For each relevant biomarker, explain specifically: the value entered, the threshold, and what it means biologically in the context of this infection. This should read as a connected clinical narrative, not a bullet dump.]

Clinical Implications — What is happening in the patient's body?
[Describe the internal physiological process — immune response, inflammatory cascade, organ involvement, etc.]

First Line of Action
[What should the patient/clinician do immediately?]

Contagiousness
- Contagious: Yes / No / Conditionally
- Contagiousness Scale: [X]/10
- Reasoning: [Brief explanation of transmission risk]

Precautions
[List of precautions to limit spread or protect the patient]

---

SOURCES
[Numbered list of cited biomedical sources — PubMed, WHO, clinical guidelines, peer-reviewed journals only. Each prediction must have at least one source. each source must be a link to the paper available online]

---

